names>AC</given-names></name><name><surname>Mercadante</surname><given-names>MT</given-names></name><name><surname>Busatto</surname><given-names>GF</given-names></name><name><surname>Miguel</surname><given-names>EC</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Obsessive-compulsive disorder in Tourette syndrome</article-title><source>Adv Neurol</source><year>2006</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>22</fpage><lpage>38</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16536350</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Denckla</surname><given-names>MB</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Attention deficit hyperactivity disorder: the childhood co-morbidity that most influences the disability burden in Tourette syndrome</article-title><source>Adv Neurol</source><year>2006</year><volume>99</volume><fpage>17</fpage><lpage>21</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16536349</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bloch</surname><given-names>MH</given-names></name><name><surname>Sukhodolsky</surname><given-names>DG</given-names></name><name><surname>Leckman</surname><given-names>JF</given-names></name><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fine-motor skill deficits in childhood predict adulthood tic severity and global psychosocial functioning in Tourette's syndrome</article-title><source>J Child Psychol Psychiatry</source><year>2006</year><volume>47</volume><fpage>551</fpage><lpage>559</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16712631</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1111/j.1469-7610.2005.01561.x</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schultz</surname><given-names>RT</given-names></name><name><surname>Carter</surname><given-names>AS</given-names></name><name><surname>Gl